PATCH 259: the per-frame BACKGROUND-TASK ROTATOR FUN_0000_461b -- FAR-vector-through-DGROUP base-loss
(SIGSEGV) reached once the object UPDATE walk (patches 243-258) completes a frame and 459a runs its
render tail.

459a's frame loop (asm 0x45b4-0x4612) ends each frame with: c0ca (update walk) -> 461b (this rotator)
-> then 4603 lcall [0x52c] -> 4607 lcall f69:12dc (scheduler) -> 460c call 22dd (the render dispatch).
461b was the immediate crash after the update walk was made crash-free.

ASM-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): 461b increments word[DGROUP:0x6ce8] and
`lcall [dword DGROUP:(0x6cea + (n&7)*4)]` -- a round-robin over an 8-entry FAR-vector table at
DGROUP:0x6cea.  Ghidra treated the table address as a host pointer, read only the low word, and emitted
a NEAR call, so *puVar1 wild-dereffed -> SIGSEGV.  Rebuilt as the faithful FAR dispatch through the
DGROUP table.  The 8 task slots are not registered on this cascade path (the table is 0), so
fist_icall_far(0) honest-traps (no-op return, the established "uninstalled vector" convention) and the
frame proceeds to 22dd.  Populating the background-task list is deferred.  Mission-cascade only.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -13385,11 +13385,19 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_461b(void)
 
 {
-  undefined2 *puVar1;
-  
